When I cloned sonic to write the patch, I found upstream already has
the fix. I should have checked this before I offered to file it.
Commit bf12ab8, "MAP_ANON should be set to -1 , not required on Linux,
required on BSD. + go fmt", by Gregory Boddin, was merged to main on
2026-09-26. It makes the same change as our vendor patch. No tag
includes it yet; the newest loader release is loader/v0.5.2, from
2026-07-30, which is the version the port uses.

An issue would duplicate a fixed bug, and a PR would duplicate a
merged commit, so I have not posted either. v3 instead cites the
upstream commit in the patch header, in an "Obtained from:" line. A
dry run of the patch against loader/v0.5.2 still applies cleanly. The
patch can go once signoz requires a loader release that includes the
fix. Nothing is left to file.

